# int-04c corpus bytes per G7's own definition (DEMONSTRATION_DESIGN.md section 4 G7). $PY=/home/usain/.cache/gov-bridge/venv/bin/python (Python 3.12.3)
# G7 text: 'Let corpus be the included text bytes of the view at the demonstration build (the build manifest's coverage). The measured
#   value is about 77.3 MB for the three named refs, per SO-04.'
# Finding: the build manifest's own 'coverage' field is a placeholder -- {'note': 'coverage is computed by govbridge.core.corpus; not duplicated in the build manifest body'}
#   so 'the build manifest's coverage' carries no number; the corpus figure must be recomputed. Two readings, both measured:
## (1) method A: from the store (blob x occurrence), distinct blobs occurring at the three NAMED refs (records 7bd7598c, product 3c880d80, evidence 58219d56)
   effect=EXCLUDE is_text=0 blobs=283 bytes=7591323
   effect=INCLUDE is_text=1 blobs=3426 bytes=45734493
   effect=LEXICAL_ONLY is_text=1 blobs=2980 bytes=39378639
   effect=METADATA_ONLY is_text=0 blobs=1 bytes=1440703
   effect=METADATA_ONLY is_text=1 blobs=5 bytes=24860731
  corpus_INCLUDE (coverage.py's own "included" = effect INCLUDE): 45734493 bytes in 3426 blobs; 1% = 457344
  corpus_INDEXED_TEXT (INCLUDE + LEXICAL_ONLY, every indexed text blob): 85113132 bytes in 6406 blobs; 1% = 851131
## (2) method B (independent of the store): git ls-tree of the three named commits, classified with config/corpus-rules.yaml via govbridge.core.corpus (the coverage command's own classifier), union by blob id
  union INCLUDE blobs 3426 bytes 45734493 | union INCLUDE+LEXICAL_ONLY blobs 6406 bytes 85113132
## per-ref coverage (int-02e): records included_bytes 43,120,206; product 38,289,514; evidence 38,324,373; unclassified 0 on all 98 refs
## Used below: corpus = union of effect-INCLUDE text bytes over the three named refs (coverage.py's own 'included', G7's three named refs).
##   The broader INCLUDE+LEXICAL_ONLY reading is reported alongside; the 77.3 MB SO-04 figure matches neither today's tree exactly.
